{
  "path": "lua/common/kdtreebox3d.lua",
  "module": "K-d tree for 3D boxes (xmin, ymin, zmin, xmax, ymax, zmax), i.e. 6 dimensions. Allows quick retrieval of all the elements whose box intersects a query box. Same API as kdtreebox2d in 3D: new -> preLoad -> build -> query/queryNotNested; export/import to reuse a tree.",
  "usage": "local kdTreeB3d = require('kdtreebox3d')\nlocal kdT = kdTreeB3d.new(itemCount)\nkdT:preLoad(id, xmin, ymin, zmin, xmax, ymax, zmax)\nkdT:build()\nfor id in kdT:queryNotNested(xmin, ymin, zmin, xmax, ymax, zmax) do ... end",
  "notes": [
    "Each element occupies 7 values in self.items (xmin, ymin, zmin, xmax, ymax, zmax, id); before build() itemCount counts values, after build() it is the number of elements.",
    "Same rules as kdtreebox2d: queryNotNested reuses the tree's state (no nesting), query allocates a state per query (nesting possible), query bounds clamped to ±1.7e308.",
    "Unlike kdtreebox2d, there is no clear() method in this version.",
    "In the code, the usage example at the top of the file describes the same calls as the 2D version; the 7-values-per-element version is what is implemented."
  ],
  "fields": {},
  "functions": {
    "new": {
      "desc": "Creates an empty 3D box k-d tree.",
      "params": {
        "itemCount": {
          "type": "integer|nil",
          "desc": "expected number of elements (preallocation, optional)"
        }
      },
      "returns": [
        {
          "type": "kdTree",
          "desc": "empty tree"
        }
      ],
      "internal": false
    }
  },
  "classes": {
    "kdTree": {
